WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.470
He's the best there is at what he does.

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:05.380
And what he does is design MCU characters.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.920
A set of renderings of Wolverine drawn by
former Disney artist Jason Pastrana in 2017

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:15.730
is making the rounds on the internet in anticipation
of the X-Man's eventual introduction to the

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.940
Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:21.980
Several pieces were posted to Pastrana's Instagram,
and while it's far from the only Marvel concept

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.860
art on his page, his reimagined movie Wolverine
may be the most intriguing.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.980
Disney didn't officially acquire the film
and television assets of Fox Studios until

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:34.150
earlier this year, so at the time this artwork
was commissioned, the notion of the X-Men

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.900
entering the MCU was not much more than speculation.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.220
Even so, Pastrana went to the trouble of designing
at least nine different takes on Wolverine’s

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.370
iconic mask, and you'll notice that all of
them downplay the parts of the mask resembling

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.160
the points of his hair, which sometimes seem
to stretch on into infinity in some of the

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.860
character's comic book depictions.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:54.900
It's worth noting the two "stealth" variants
with the mouth and nose covered, a version

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:59.420
with an X on the forehead, and the presence
of a great, big, stinky stogie in every version

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.640
where the mouth is visible.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.900
Odds are Disney would have nixed that detail.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.510
Pastrana eventually settled on a version he
liked, something of a combination between

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:11.020
the designs numbered 2 and 5, and designed
the entire costume, front and back.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.940
As iconic as Hugh Jackman's long run as Wolverine
in the Fox-produced movies was, the character

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.540
has never even come close to looking like
this in a movie.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.320
"You actually go outside in these things?"

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.800
"Well, what would you prefer?

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.800
Yellow spandex?"

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.600
This version of Wolverine is a lot closer
to what we're familiar with from the comics.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.320
He looks older, downright grizzled, as if
the MCU version of Wolverine would start out

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.700
as aged and haggard as the one in Logan rather
than ending there.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.540
The rendering of the face even looks a little
bit like Jackman.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.271
It's enough to make you wonder if, at some
point, Disney execs were kicking around the

00:01:44.271 --> 00:01:49.150
notion of porting over the Fox version of
the X-Men to the MCU before deciding to recast

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.540
everyone except Deadpool.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.240
"Hey!

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:53.080
It's me!

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.320
Don't scratch!

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.540
Just cleanin' up the timelines!"

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:01.980
Since Pastrana drew these concepts in 2017,
names that have been bandied about as possible

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.770
successors to Jackman skew much younger than
the depictions here look: Rocketman's Taron

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.260
Egerton, Dacre Montgomery from Stranger Things,
and even Daniel Radcliffe of Harry Potter

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.939
fame have all been rumored to be considered
for Wolverine.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:16.880
But Pastrana's work is definitely worth consideration.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.840
It seems to be a clever way to fit Logan into
the MCU.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.760
Note the compact, streamlined look of the
helmet and the utilitarian feel of the uniform,

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.909
which evokes an aesthetic similar to the duds
worn by agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. or superheroes

00:02:28.909 --> 00:02:30.320
with a more militaristic bent.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:34.739
There's even a sort of belt pouch, or, if
we're being less charitable, a fanny pack,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:35.900
with a little "X" on it.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.560
It's not hard to imagine another MCU character
making some kind of wisecrack about that.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.340
"What are you wearing?"

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:43.349
"Oh, I always wear this.

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:44.180
This is one of my favorites."

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.379
Pastrana apparently does this kind of stuff
all the time, and if you visit his Instagram,

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.280
you will absolutely get lost in it.

00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:56.560
Other designs of his include an MCU version
of Doctor Doom, a rendering of Riri Williams,

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.349
better known as Ironheart, and a version of
Spider-Man if his suit had been designed not

00:03:00.349 --> 00:03:02.019
by Tony Stark, but by Shuri.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.939
It'd definitely be cool if at least some elements
of Pastrana's design make it to the big screen,

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:10.900
because, again, it's a version of Wolverine
who seems to fit the MCU aesthetic.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.670
We have the distinct feeling that he'd do
the team justice if he were to put his mind

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.950
to designing their MCU look because, what
do you know, he already did it, and it's a

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.000
really smart take.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:24.340
That said, Pastrana doesn't work for Disney
anymore, so it's more than likely another

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.640
concept artist will provide their own designs
for Marvel's mutants.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.860
And we'll have to wait several years to find
out if the characters' eventual designs resemble

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:35.260
Pastrana's handiwork or go into an entirely
different direction.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:40.020
Marvel Studios has not announced the release
dates of any X-Men projects as of yet.

